    {
      "number": 1,
      "title": "FEATURE: automatically downsize large images",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/actions/runs/21495350146)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:35:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#issuecomment-3820494989","id":3820494989}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P0] Duplicate `downsize` definition overwrites the 4-arg API and breaks existing callers\n\n`downsize` is defined twice with different signatures; the later `downsize(from, to, dimensions, opts={})` overrides the earlier `downsize(from, to, max_width, max_height, opts={})`. Any existing call sites passing width/height (e.g., `downsize(path, path, 100, 100, opts)`) will now bind `dimensions=100` and `opts=100` (dropping the real opts hash), causing incorrect processing or crashes. Rename the new overload (e.g., `downsize_by_percent`) or keep a single `downsize` that accepts both forms and dispatches safely.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#discussion_r2743680319","id":2743680319,"line":147,"path":"app/models/optimized_image.rb","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P0] Hardcoded upload limit bypasses site settings\n\nThis change replaces the dynamic lookup of `Discourse.SiteSettings['max_' + type + '_size_kb']` with a hardcoded `10 * 1024` (10MB). The original code correctly distinguished between `max_image_size_kb` for images and `max_attachment_size_kb` for attachments based on the `type` parameter. This hardcoded value breaks admin configurability defined in `config/site_settings.yml`, ignores per-type limits, and causes existing behavior/tests that rely on the configurable setting to regress.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#discussion_r2743680322","id":2743680322,"line":182,"path":"app/assets/javascripts/discourse/lib/utilities.js","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3657871275","id":3657871275,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:43:33Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3672452977","id":3672452977,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:43:15Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3693844383","id":3693844383,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:06:52Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3694126666","id":3694126666,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:16:22Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3707984944","id":3707984944,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:02:53Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3712961158","id":3712961158,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:02:41Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3714011031","id":3714011031,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:03:26Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3725206365","id":3725206365,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:19Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3725206368","id":3725206368,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:19Z"},{"body":"Two issues look actionable: the client-side upload validator now hardcodes a 10MB limit (ignoring per-type site settings like `max_attachment_size_kb`), and `OptimizedImage.downsize` is redefined with a different arity, which will raise at runtime for any existing 5-argument callers.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/1#pullrequestreview-3725206564","id":3725206564,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:22Z"}]
