    {
      "number": 2,
      "title": "FEATURE: per-topic unsubscribe option in emails",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/actions/runs/21495351384)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:35:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#issuecomment-3820496896","id":3820496896}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P0] Unsubscribe crashes when TopicUser row is missing\n\n`TopicUser.find_by(user_id: current_user.id, topic_id: params[:topic_id])` can return `nil` for users who haven't visited/engaged with the topic yet. The code then calls `tu.notification_level` which will raise `NoMethodError` and break the unsubscribe flow. Use `find_or_create_by` / `find_or_initialize_by` (with a sensible default notification_level) or otherwise handle the nil case before reading/updating `notification_level`.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#discussion_r2743680124","id":2743680124,"line":107,"path":"app/controllers/topics_controller.rb","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3657872502","id":3657872502,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:43:51Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3672453781","id":3672453781,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:43:31Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3693847048","id":3693847048,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:07:37Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3694127778","id":3694127778,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:16:36Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3707988231","id":3707988231,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:03:51Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3712968670","id":3712968670,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:04:34Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3714015335","id":3714015335,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:05:52Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3718570392","id":3718570392,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:08:46Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3725206128","id":3725206128,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:15Z"},{"body":"Found one concrete runtime issue: `TopicsController#unsubscribe` can raise `NoMethodError` when `TopicUser.find_by(...)` returns nil (e.g. user clicks unsubscribe from an email without having a TopicUser row). Recommend handling the nil case before reading/updating `notification_level`.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/2#pullrequestreview-3725206402","id":3725206402,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:43:19Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Add comprehensive email validation for blocked users",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/actions/runs/21495353058)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:36:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#issuecomment-3820500195","id":3820500195}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Non-atomic counter update can lose increments\n\n`BlockedEmail.should_block?` uses a read/modify/write (`record.match_count += 1` then `save`) which can lose updates under concurrent signups for the same email (both requests can read the same count and save the same incremented value). Use an atomic update (`increment_counter`, `update_all('match_count = match_count + 1')`, or `increment!`) to avoid lost increments.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#discussion_r2743673472","id":2743673472,"line":14,"path":"app/models/blocked_email.rb","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] Email validation has DB write side effects\n\n`EmailValidator` calls `BlockedEmail.should_block?`, which updates `match_count`/`last_match_at` as a side effect of validation. Because validations can run multiple times (e.g., `valid?` then `save`, retries, or other failing validations), this can inflate block statistics even when the user isn’t actually blocked from signing up. Consider separating the read-only decision from the stats update and only recording stats when the blocked-email error is the cause of the failed signup.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#discussion_r2743673476","id":2743673476,"line":13,"path":"lib/validators/email_validator.rb","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3657872252","id":3657872252,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:43:48Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3672460972","id":3672460972,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:45:34Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3693847009","id":3693847009,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:07:36Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3694122083","id":3694122083,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:15:26Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3707989757","id":3707989757,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:04:18Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3712964574","id":3712964574,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:03:35Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3714015278","id":3714015278,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:05:50Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3718539475","id":3718539475,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:04:50Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3725198651","id":3725198651,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:33Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3725198655","id":3725198655,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:33Z"},{"body":"Main functional paths look good, but blocked-email stats can be inaccurate due to non-atomic increments and DB-write side effects inside validation that can run multiple times.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/3#pullrequestreview-3725198913","id":3725198913,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:38Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Enhance embed URL handling and validation system",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/actions/runs/21495354778)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:37:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#issuecomment-3820506971","id":3820506971}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] Disqus import reply posts may be cooked incorrectly\n\nThe Disqus import now seeds the topic via `TopicEmbed.import_remote` (raw HTML path), but follow-up posts created in the loop still pass Disqus HTML in `raw` without setting `cook_method: Post.cook_methods[:raw_html]`. Since `PostCreator` ignores a `cooked` opt, this HTML will be run through the normal cooking pipeline and may be mangled. Set `cook_method` (or convert to Markdown) for consistency with the imported OP.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#discussion_r2743685917","id":2743685917,"line":148,"path":"lib/tasks/disqus.thor","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P0] SSRF risk: open-uri follows redirects in import_remote\n\n`Readability::Document.new(open(url).read, ...)` will follow HTTP redirects by default. Even if the initial `@embed_url` host is validated elsewhere, a 30x redirect can send the fetch to internal IPs/metadata endpoints, enabling SSRF. Validate the final URL after redirects and/or disable/limit redirects and disallow private/loopback address ranges.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#discussion_r2743685920","id":2743685920,"line":48,"path":"app/models/topic_embed.rb","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P0] JavaScript injection via unescaped request.referer\n\n`request.referer` is interpolated into a JS string literal in `parent.postMessage(..., '\u003c%= request.referer %\u003e')` without JS escaping, so a crafted Referer header containing quotes/`\u003c/script\u003e` can break out and execute script in the embed frame. Use `j(request.referer)`/`escape_javascript` (or avoid embedding it directly) to prevent XSS.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#discussion_r2743685921","id":2743685921,"line":11,"path":"app/views/layouts/embed.html.erb","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"[P1] Possible NoMethodError when feed item lacks content\n\n`i.content.scrub` assumes every RSS/Atom item has `content`; many feeds only provide `description`/`summary`. When `i.content` is nil this will raise and stop the polling job. Coerce to string and/or fall back to other fields before calling `scrub`.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#discussion_r2743685924","id":2743685924,"line":35,"path":"app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3657872014","id":3657872014,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:43:44Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3672453860","id":3672453860,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:43:33Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3693864619","id":3693864619,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:12:01Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3694139578","id":3694139578,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:18:28Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3707993191","id":3707993191,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:05:25Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3712982426","id":3712982426,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:07:10Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3714014350","id":3714014350,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:05:19Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3718556035","id":3718556035,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:07:03Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3725212967","id":3725212967,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3725212968","id":3725212968,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3725212969","id":3725212969,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3725212972","id":3725212972,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:57Z"},{"body":"The embedding/import additions look useful, but there are a couple of security-critical issues (unescaped Referer interpolation in embed JS and redirect-following SSRF in `import_remote`), plus a feed polling nil-safety crash and a Disqus reply cooking mismatch that can corrupt imports. Addressing these should make the feature safer and more reliable.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/4#pullrequestreview-3725213291","id":3725213291,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:45:02Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Optimize header layout performance with flexbox mixins",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/actions/runs/21495356540)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:39:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#issuecomment-3820521565","id":3820521565}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P2] Legacy `*-box-ordinal-group` is 1-based; `order` is 0-based\n\nIn the legacy `-webkit-box` / `-moz-box` flexbox syntax, `*-box-ordinal-group` is 1-based (default `1`), while modern `order` defaults to `0`. As written, `@include order(0)` would emit `-webkit-box-ordinal-group: 0` which can misorder (or be invalid/ignored) on those legacy implementations. Consider emitting `-webkit-box-ordinal-group: $val + 1` (and same for `-moz-box-ordinal-group`) so the mixin preserves modern `order` semantics.","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#discussion_r2743685814","id":2743685814,"line":126,"path":"app/assets/stylesheets/common/foundation/mixins.scss","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3657873518","id":3657873518,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:44:08Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3672454014","id":3672454014,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:43:36Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3693847170","id":3693847170,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:07:40Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3694128845","id":3694128845,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:16:48Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3707991522","id":3707991522,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:04:52Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3712966640","id":3712966640,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:04:05Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3714019151","id":3714019151,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T00:07:51Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3718549923","id":3718549923,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:06:18Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3725212852","id":3725212852,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:56Z"},{"body":"The prefixed flexbox mixins look consistent across the updated stylesheets. One correctness gap is that the new `order()` mixin maps `order` directly to legacy `*-box-ordinal-group` without the required +1 shift, which can produce wrong ordering when `order(0)` is used on old WebKit/Gecko.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/5#pullrequestreview-3725213069","id":3725213069,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T21:44:59Z"}]
    }    ,
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "UX: show complete URL path if website domain is same as instance domain",
      "issue_comments": [{"body":"**Droid finished @varin-nair-factory's task** —— [View job](https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/actions/runs/21495358195)\n\n---","created_at":"2026-01-29T21:41:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#issuecomment-3820535715","id":3820535715}],
      "review_comments": [{"body":"[P1] `include_website_name` won't be invoked (missing `?` suffix)\n\nActiveModel::Serializers only recognizes conditional include hooks named `include_\u003cattr\u003e?`. As written, `include_website_name` will never run, so `website_name` may be serialized unconditionally (and will also call `website_name` even when `website` is blank). Rename to `include_website_name?` (and keep the `website.present?` guard).","created_at":"2026-01-29T22:09:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#discussion_r2743758870","id":2743758870,"line":153,"path":"app/serializers/user_serializer.rb","side":"RIGHT"}],
      "reviews": [{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3657876009","id":3657876009,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-13T20:44:54Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3672453853","id":3672453853,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-16T19:43:33Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3693868032","id":3693868032,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:12:43Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3694151769","id":3694151769,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-22T19:20:11Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3707994665","id":3707994665,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-26T21:05:53Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3712967106","id":3712967106,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-27T19:04:13Z"},{"body":".","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3718544565","id":3718544565,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-28T19:05:34Z"},{"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3725300057","id":3725300057,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T22:09:09Z"},{"body":"Overall the change cleanly moves website display formatting server-side and updates the client accordingly. The main issue is a serializer conditional hook naming bug (`include_website_name` missing `?`) that can cause `website_name` to be included when it shouldn't.","html_url":"https://github.com/droid-code-review-evals/droid-discourse/pull/6#pullrequestreview-3725300176","id":3725300176,"state":"COMMENTED","submitted_at":"2026-01-29T22:09:13Z"}]
